Error [jet.TypestateWrongState]: `receipt` needs `Order.Shipped`, but `o` is `Order.Draft`
  --> tests/ui/typestate/state_type_argument_in_wrong_state.jet:22:19
    |
 22 |     print(receipt(o))
    |                   ^
 Why: Typestate: `receipt` takes only `Order.Shipped`; calling it with `Order` in another state is the out-of-order bug the state list rules out
 Fix: Moves from `Order.Draft`: `confirm`, `cancel`
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E0150
